01:53:29.236 --> 01:53:30.792
- [Connor] Yeah, exactly, that's it.

01:53:30.792 --> 01:53:32.534
- And I didn't realize that until after

01:53:32.534 --> 01:53:34.435
university life had ended,

01:53:34.435 --> 01:53:36.537
that we were just really lucky,

01:53:36.537 --> 01:53:40.860
as a kid, as a teenager,
whatever, to just,

01:53:40.860 --> 01:53:42.860
every year you'd kind
of get a new experience.

01:53:42.860 --> 01:53:45.320
But, once that period
of your life is over,

01:53:45.320 --> 01:53:47.060
then you just have to
search for that yourself

01:53:47.060 --> 01:53:47.940
and it's just not gonna come to you,

01:53:47.940 --> 01:53:49.680
you gotta do that yourself.

01:53:49.680 --> 01:53:51.900
And that's why I feel like a lotta people

01:53:51.900 --> 01:53:54.420
who we, in the same area
who we grew up with,

01:53:54.420 --> 01:53:56.440
they just didn't end up
staying in that same area.

01:53:56.440 --> 01:53:57.434
Or they just,

01:53:57.434 --> 01:53:59.890
you go back home and they
haven't changed much, right?

01:53:59.890 --> 01:54:02.750
And that's just because
they haven't realized that

01:54:02.750 --> 01:54:03.620
if they don't do something,

01:54:03.620 --> 01:54:04.610
then nothing's ever gonna change

01:54:04.610 --> 01:54:05.780
and some people are comfortable with that.

01:54:05.780 --> 01:54:06.750
And that's completely fine.

01:54:06.750 --> 01:54:08.160
But I think there are,

01:54:08.160 --> 01:54:09.795
I've met enough people in my life who

01:54:09.795 --> 01:54:14.070
have like this urge to do something new

01:54:14.070 --> 01:54:15.847
and do something different

01:54:15.847 --> 01:54:16.760
but don't even know where to get started.

01:54:16.760 --> 01:54:17.970
- You should go for it.

01:54:17.970 --> 01:54:19.341
- And I feel like, just go for it.

01:54:19.341 --> 01:54:20.174
Just do you-

01:54:20.174 --> 01:54:21.300
- You miss every shot
you don't take, right?

01:54:21.300 --> 01:54:22.400
- Yeah, yeah.
- That's like it.

01:54:22.400 --> 01:54:23.577
- Just do something out
of your comfort zone.

01:54:23.577 --> 01:54:24.590
- Yeah, at some point.

01:54:24.590 --> 01:54:26.030
- Yeah, you don't need
an excuse to do anything.

01:54:26.030 --> 01:54:27.380
- Yeah, just take a risk.

01:54:27.380 --> 01:54:28.820
- I remember, one time, my friend went

01:54:28.820 --> 01:54:29.938
and traveled abroad alone.

01:54:29.938 --> 01:54:32.250
And I was like, "Wow. What the fuck?

01:54:32.250 --> 01:54:33.083
You can do that?"

01:54:33.083 --> 01:54:34.436
(Joey laughs)

01:54:34.436 --> 01:54:35.790
"Just go somewhere for fun, alone?"

01:54:35.790 --> 01:54:37.560
And I remember I thought, "Okay.

01:54:37.560 --> 01:54:39.223
I'm kinda jealous that this guy

01:54:39.223 --> 01:54:40.260
just had the balls to do that."

01:54:40.260 --> 01:54:41.905
And now, I wouldn't mind doing that.

01:54:41.905 --> 01:54:42.738
I'd do it.

01:54:42.738 --> 01:54:43.860
I wouldn't, it's not preferable.

01:54:43.860 --> 01:54:44.940
But I wouldn't mind doing it.

01:54:44.940 --> 01:54:46.782
If I wanna go somewhere,
or you wanna do something,

01:54:46.782 --> 01:54:47.848
you don't need an excuse to do it.

01:54:47.848 --> 01:54:49.190
Just fuckin' go somewhere.
- Just do it.

01:54:49.190 --> 01:54:50.270
- I always thought, I remember,

01:54:50.270 --> 01:54:53.435
I was talking to a guy who had,

01:54:53.435 --> 01:54:54.907
back in university,

01:54:54.907 --> 01:54:56.511
he was talking about,

01:54:56.511 --> 01:54:58.520
this was a guy in his 30s,

01:54:58.520 --> 01:54:59.353
he was talking about,

01:54:59.353 --> 01:55:01.047
"Yeah, I used to work at this big company.

01:55:01.047 --> 01:55:04.240
And then I just quit. And saved up.

01:55:04.240 --> 01:55:05.407
And just traveled, for
like a year or two."

01:55:05.407 --> 01:55:06.963
And I'm just like, "Wait.

01:55:07.919 --> 01:55:08.810
I thought gap years were,

01:55:08.810 --> 01:55:10.780
I thought you could do
that after your gap years.

01:55:10.780 --> 01:55:11.880
That's what gap years were for."

01:55:11.880 --> 01:55:13.153
And he's just like, "No,

01:55:13.153 --> 01:55:16.210
I just did it because I just
needed change in my life."

01:55:16.210 --> 01:55:17.696
And you're like, "Wait,

01:55:17.696 --> 01:55:19.939
but what happens when you go back?

01:55:19.939 --> 01:55:22.345
What, you have a career, right?"

01:55:22.345 --> 01:55:26.390
I just couldn't comprehend
someone just doing

01:55:26.390 --> 01:55:27.830
something out of

01:55:28.761 --> 01:55:30.900
the life path that, you know,

01:55:30.900 --> 01:55:32.716
the career path that I was taught."

01:55:32.716 --> 01:55:33.930
- [Connor] You can do everything.

01:55:33.930 --> 01:55:35.500
- It's like, yeah, the
moment you have your career,

01:55:35.500 --> 01:55:36.650
it's like, "Why would you willingly

01:55:36.650 --> 01:55:38.927
just end your career like that?"

01:55:38.927 --> 01:55:40.650
- (laughs) Why would you just
quit your job like that? Ugh.

01:55:40.650 --> 01:55:42.078
- Yeah.

01:55:42.078 --> 01:55:43.920
- But, I mean, yeah. Fuck.

01:55:43.920 --> 01:55:45.820
If I was in that position, I'd
probably do it too, you know?

01:55:45.820 --> 01:55:50.320
And sometimes it does take that
kind of massive risk-taking

01:55:50.320 --> 01:55:53.090
to realize that, "Oh,
maybe it's fuckin' worth it

01:55:53.090 --> 01:55:53.923
to end your career.

01:55:53.923 --> 01:55:55.283
Maybe that career wasn't worth it."

01:55:55.283 --> 01:55:57.278
- I'm gonna end my career.
- Be a YouTuber.

01:55:57.278 --> 01:55:58.404
- Yeah, YouTubers be like.

01:55:58.404 --> 01:55:59.830
- Just be a YouTuber.
- YouTubers be like.

01:55:59.830 --> 01:56:00.832
(all laugh)

01:56:00.832 --> 01:56:01.800
- I'm just gonna end my career.

01:56:01.800 --> 01:56:03.576
- I'm just gonna end my
career. Go on a trip.

01:56:03.576 --> 01:56:06.380
- Yeah, but I feel like
especially this goes to most

01:56:06.380 --> 01:56:08.520
high schoolers, because I feel like that's

01:56:08.520 --> 01:56:10.206
the point in your life where
you have the most opportunity

01:56:10.206 --> 01:56:14.190
to do something crazy with your life.

01:56:14.190 --> 01:56:15.023
Not even something crazy,

01:56:15.023 --> 01:56:16.730
just something outta your comfort zone.

01:56:16.730 --> 01:56:18.810
Something that can increase
your perspective of

01:56:18.810 --> 01:56:20.747
what happens in the world.
- Just try some shit out,

01:56:20.747 --> 01:56:21.580
if it doesn't work out,

01:56:21.580 --> 01:56:22.790
try some different shit, until it clicks.

01:56:22.790 --> 01:56:25.531
- Yeah, if you're about to go
to university at some point,

01:56:25.531 --> 01:56:27.560
and you might be looking
for courses or whatever,

01:56:27.560 --> 01:56:29.410
dude, look around for international stuff,

01:56:29.410 --> 01:56:30.860
whatever, there's tons out there.

01:56:30.860 --> 01:56:32.210
- Anything that interests you.
- It'll be fun as fuck.

01:56:32.210 --> 01:56:33.133
- Yeah. Trust me.

01:56:33.133 --> 01:56:37.110
I remember, the biggest
adventure I'd gone on

01:56:37.110 --> 01:56:39.470
is just moving cities to
go to my university town

01:56:39.470 --> 01:56:43.720
and in England, every
city's kind of the same.

01:56:43.720 --> 01:56:45.560
You get the same kinda experience,

01:56:45.560 --> 01:56:47.810
you get freshers week,
you go drink a fuckton,

01:56:47.810 --> 01:56:50.150
it's the same, (laughs) it
was like the same experience

01:56:50.150 --> 01:56:52.321
no matter what university
I would've gone to.

01:56:52.321 --> 01:56:54.640
And I wish I studied abroad.

01:56:54.640 --> 01:56:56.930
I wish I'd done something new.

01:56:56.930 --> 01:56:59.400
And I feel like,

01:56:59.400 --> 01:57:01.071
after I quit to become a YouTuber,

01:57:01.071 --> 01:57:03.813
I was gaining back the
years that I could've had

01:57:03.813 --> 01:57:06.690
if I'd just gone out of my
comfort zone earlier in my life.

01:57:06.690 --> 01:57:08.300
- Yeah, I've definitely been doing that,

01:57:08.300 --> 01:57:11.530
since I've gotten so many
opportunities doing this job,

01:57:11.530 --> 01:57:14.180
I feel like I'm just
playing a catch-up game,

01:57:14.180 --> 01:57:16.040
I'm taking literally every thing

01:57:16.040 --> 01:57:17.460
that comes to my doorstep now,

01:57:17.460 --> 01:57:20.250
because I didn't take any
of that shit, back then.

01:57:20.250 --> 01:57:21.083
- Yeah. Same, same.

01:57:21.083 --> 01:57:22.670
- So and now I regret it.

01:57:22.670 --> 01:57:23.520
Being like, "Oh, fuck.

01:57:23.520 --> 01:57:26.600
Why was I so lazy and
dumb to not take these,

01:57:26.600 --> 01:57:27.630
now that I look at it,

01:57:27.630 --> 01:57:29.340
